      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T07:13:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review! Addressing the 3 points\n\n1. Why use this specific function? \n   - While I cannot find a good documentation on this, but from [Android doc](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Context#sendBroadcastAsUser(android.content.Intent,%20android.os.UserHandle)), **\"This is not available to applications that are not pre-installed on the system image\"** to me sounds correct to be in a system stack\n   - As mentioned, `sendBroadcastAsUser` is repeatly used in [HeadsetService](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java;l\u003d2408?q\u003dsendbroadcastasuser%20headset) and [HeadsetStatemachine](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetStateMachine.java;l\u003d355). Tracing the code, it has been [added to address specifically a multi-user issue](http://ag/586032). This sounds like the right solution for the specific scenario I am facing. As HFP is the only path that is working with Telecom right now.\n   \n2. Is Broadcast receiver correctly configured to receive the intents?\n  - I think so, Telecom state receiver specifically [filtered](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/services/Telecomm/src/com/android/server/telecom/bluetooth/BluetoothStateReceiver.java;l\u003d83?q\u003dbluetoothstate%20receiver\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain) these intents. It works for Headset but not LE Audio and hearing aid.\n  - I guess we can also fix this by using `registerReceiverForAllUsers` in Telecom. But again, I see that headset already uses `sendBroadcastAsUser` so it makes more sense to me here.\n  \n3. Telecom refactor\n  - I did try enabling their flag (`use_refactored_audio_route_switching`). Still does not work. And I see that they did not touch the intent receiver yet.",
